<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gabriel García Moreno</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1821">1821</a>–<a href="/years/1875">1875</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gabriel García Moreno was twice president of Ecuador, from 1861 to 1865 and from 1869 until his assassination in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> in 1875. A conservative Catholic, he signed a concordat with the Vatican, dedicated the country to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacred-heart">Sacred Heart</a> and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> a condition of citizenship, while also building roads, schools and the Quito observatory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gabriel-garcia-moreno.jpg" alt="Gabriel García Moreno" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Presidencia de la República del Ecuador · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gabriel_Garc%C3%ADa_Moreno.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the crisis of 1859–1860, when the country split among rival governments and Peru blockaded Guayaquil, <b>Gabriel García Moreno</b> and Flores retook the port in September 1860 and restored a single government.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-ecuador">Republic of Ecuador · Military</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/ecuador">Ecuador</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/ecuador">Ecuador</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-2.19,-79.89&amp;year=1856" aria-label="Guayaquil on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2332 2246 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Gabriel García Moreno"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2782 2516h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2782 2516h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-2.19,-79.89&amp;year=1856">What was here in 1856? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
